The retained admission and branch records below are immutable lineage statements, not present-tense execution authority. Their original wording is preserved to avoid rewriting history. Every current reader must interpret `open`, `active`, `admitted`, `mutable`, and equivalent wording below as scoped to the named historical branch or gate only.

New retained records should use explicit dates, branch or gate identifiers, status, scope, and completion-claim limits so that historical execution truth cannot be mistaken for a current route. Historical evidence may explain why a surface exists; it cannot establish that the surface is currently correct, admitted, mutable, or complete.

