# Parallel Workflow Control Repair 1 — PM Record

## Status

`REPAIRED_CANDIDATE_AWAITING_INDEPENDENT_CONTROL_TEST`

This record does not accept the repaired control checkpoint and does not authorise any lane launch. It records the bounded repairs made after the PM self-audit rejection.

## Repairs made

- admitted seven durable parallel-control concepts through M15 human vocabulary governance and regenerated the deterministic canonical projection;
- changed full-read law to require a current-target control manifest or assignment-local lane manifest inside each authorised evidence directory;
- added the test-subtree override and its exact authority sequence to Lane 1AW and Lane 1AT;
- fixed assignment revision `R1`, exact Worker Candidate Archive names and exact tester verdict package names;
- defined the Tester-approved Portability Artefact and its mandatory package members, bundle and reconstruction proof;
- expanded the workflow registry for source, revision, worker/tester commits, verdict, artefact hash, PM disposition, queue, integration and aggregate validation lineage;
- removed the global registry from lane mandatory reading and stated operational rather than fictional secrecy;
- created the separate `Parallel Control T1` independent tester brief and blocked all lane launch pending tester PASS and later PM acceptance;
- superseded the original PM acceptance record and extended structural validation for the repaired obligations.

## Validation qualification

The complete two-file vocabulary test command reports two failures. The identical two node IDs fail at the exact superseded source commit `9e404df7…`: the historical `Serial Desk-cognition` heading expectation and the historical missing `mutable_runtime_surface` baseline term. The repair introduces no additional failure. Builder idempotence, committed-projection parity, three unaffected governance tests and deterministic validation of all seven new admissions pass. These pre-existing failures remain visible and are not suppressed or represented as repaired.

## Next gate

Publish one full-history repair checkpoint and issue only the `Parallel Control T1` brief. Do not create `Lane 1AW`–`Lane 4AW` yet.

